Lets Alloy-style browsers show Chromium's own pages (chrome://settings,
chrome://extensions, chrome://history...) as ordinary pages, for Arbalete,
whose tabs are all Alloy-style browsers.

- CEF (alloy_browser_host_impl.cc) refuses every chrome:// page but a short
  list. It now lets any of them load when the browser navigates to it (the
  app, on the user's request) or when another chrome:// page opens it; web
  content still reaches only the list. The app chooses which pages it opens.
- These pages expect to sit in a tab of a Chromium Browser window, which an
  Alloy-style browser is not: the handlers below look one up and crash the
  browser process when there is none. Each is guarded where a visible button
  of the pages Arbalete opens reaches it, and does nothing instead:
  - settings, About: "Get help" (about_handler.cc, ShowHelp);
  - settings, Appearance: "Customize your toolbar" (appearance_handler.cc);
  - settings, Import: the file picker's parent window (import_data_handler.cc);
  - settings, Autofill: "Google Password Manager" (password_manager_handler.cc);
  - password manager, Settings: "Manage passkeys"
    (settings_security_key_handler.cc) and "Add shortcut"
    (passwords_private_delegate_impl.cc);
  - history, Journeys: its handler, a visit's click and "Open all in new tab
    group" (history_ui.cc, history_clusters_handler.cc);
  - extensions, Details: "Extension options" (developer_private_functions.cc).

Paths are relative to Chromium's src (scripts/build.sh).

